tps://doi.org/10.1070/IM1992v039n03ABEH002243†doi.org (Mi im971)\nL45: \nL46: * * *\nL47: This article is cited in 3 scientific papers (total in 4 papers)\nL48: Multiplicative functions on the set of shifted prime numbers\nL49: cite35†N. M. Timofeev ^{}\nL50: cite36†English version PDF (706 kB) cite37†Citations (4) cite38†Russian version article References: cite39†PDF cite40†HTML DOI: cite34†https://doi.org/10.1070/IM1992v039n03ABEH002243†doi.org Abstract: This paper is concerned with the behavior of multiplicative functions on the set $\\{p+a\\}$, where $p$ is a prime and $a$ is a nonzero integer. Several results are obtained in which either the average value of a multiplicative function on this set is estimated or its asymptotic behavior is determined.\nL51: As one application a nontrivial estimate of\nL52: $$\\sum\\limits_{p\\leqslant x}\\chi_q(p+a)$$\nL53: is found, where $x\\geqslant q^{1/4+\\varepsilon}$, $q$ is a sufficiently large prime, and $\\chi$ is a character of degree greater than 4. Received: 12.02.1991 Bibliographic databases: UDC: 511.33 MSC: cite41†11A25†mathscinet.ams.org , cite42†11N37†mathscinet.ams.org Language: English Original paper language: Russian Citation: N. M. Timofeev, “Multiplicative functions on the set of shifted prime numbers”, Math. USSR-Izv., 39:3 (1992), 1189–1207 cite43†Image Citation in format cite44†AMSBIB `\\Bibitem{Tim91}\nL54: \\by N.~M.~Timofeev\nL55: \\paper Multiplicative functions on the set of shifted prime numbers\nL56: \\jour Math. USSR-Izv.\nL57: \\yr 1992\nL58: \\vol 39\nL59: \\issue 3\nL60: \\pages 1189--1207\nL61: \\mathnet{http://mi.mathnet.ru/eng/im971}\nL62: \\crossref{https://doi.org/10.1070/IM1992v039n03ABEH002243}\nL63: \\mathscinet{https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1152211}\nL64: \\zmath{https://zbmath.org/?q=an:0778.11052|0744.11044}\nL65: \\adsnasa{https://adsabs.harvard.edu/cgi-bin/bib_query?1992IzMat..39.1189T}\nL66: \\isi{https://gateway.webofknowledge